1
00:00:00,491 --> 00:00:02,491
(Sheldon:)She's smart, insightful.

2
00:00:02,660 --> 00:00:06,660
(Sheldon:)She has a very unique way of,
you know, revering me.

3
00:00:08,624 --> 00:00:13,424
- Here's your spinach-mushroom omelet.
- Thank you.

4
00:00:14,213 --> 00:00:17,003
(Sheldon:)- Did anyone touch it?
- Gloves were worn by everyone involved.

5
00:00:17,174 --> 00:00:18,384
(Ramona:)I was vigilant.

6
00:00:19,343 --> 00:00:22,183
(Sheldon:)Ramona pointed out
that I've been wasting 20 minutes a day...

7
00:00:22,346 --> 00:00:23,806
(Sheldon:)...standing on cafeteria lines.

8
00:00:23,973 --> 00:00:27,723
(Ramona:)Time which would be better spent tackling
the great physics problems of our day.

9
00:00:27,893 --> 00:00:32,393
(Sheldon:)You don't tackle the big issues, Ramona.
You fence with them. En garde. Riposte.

10
00:00:32,565 --> 00:00:33,855
[LAUGH ING]

11
00:00:37,278 --> 00:00:38,908
Touché.

12
00:00:39,947 --> 00:00:41,697
(Leonard:)- Morning.
- Oh, hey, Leslie.

13
00:00:41,866 --> 00:00:43,866
So I see you're organizing your papers...

14
00:00:44,035 --> 00:00:47,325
(Leslie:)...for the Smithsonian Museum
of Dumb-Assery.

15
00:00:48,372 --> 00:00:52,712
(Ramona:)There won't be any room until they get rid
of the permanent Leslie Winkle exhibit.

16
00:00:53,628 --> 00:00:55,758
(Sheldon:)Oh, good one.

17
00:00:56,631 --> 00:00:58,961
(Leslie:)I see you got a grad student
to fight your battles.

18
00:00:59,133 --> 00:01:02,023
(Leslie:)I'll let you keep your lunch money today.

